course: dictionary
lesson: 11071
title: Weird and wonderful
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Weird is an adjective. It means very strange or unusual, in a way that is surprising or hard to explain. You can change it to weirder and weirdest.
explain: Look at the words around it. «A weird light in the sky» tells you the light is odd, and a little scary or magical, not just an ordinary light. Ask: what word would fit here? Strange would fit, so weird means something like strange.
explain: In everyday talk, «That's weird!» means something odd just happened. But calling a person weird because they are different can hurt them, so choose your words kindly.
fact: Weird is an adjective: weird, weirder, weirdest.
fact: «Weird» means very strange or unusual, in a way that is surprising or hard to explain.
fact: «Weird» can also mean strange in a slightly scary or magical way, as in «a weird light in the sky».
fact: Scientists call some animals weird, such as the platypus, the axolotl and the anglerfish, because they show how many different ways living things can adapt.
fact: If someone online makes you feel weird or uncomfortable, trust that feeling and tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «A weird light in the sky» appeared over the field. What does weird mean here? | Bright and warm like the sun | Heavy and slow | *Strange and a little magical | Loud and cheerful
exercise: Which word is the comparative form of weird, meaning more weird? | weirded | weirdly | *weirder | weirdness
exercise: Lena sees a bird fly backwards and says, «That's weird!» What does she mean? | *That is odd and surprising | That is funny and kind | That is very quiet | That is very old
test: Calling someone weird because they are different can | make them taller | help them sleep better | *hurt them | make them rich
test: If someone online makes you feel weird or uncomfortable, what should you do? | Ignore the feeling and keep quiet | *Trust the feeling and tell a trusted adult | Hide it for a week | Send them a secret message
exam: Which sentence uses weird to mean strange in a slightly scary or magical way? | My socks are weird today. | *«A weird light in the sky hung above the wood.» | The weird bus was on time.
